#
# File rows (`itok check`): the cost of one spec file, o200k tokens.
# Dir rows (`sherd budget`): the CHAIN cost of reaching a node -- root
# plus every ancestor plus the node -- which is what an agent pays before
# it sees any code. `.` is the root node.
#
# Re-set 2026-10-03 after federating into scripts, nix and docs and
# archiving finished tasks: ~15% over the measured size (`itok estimate
# --bpe` for files, `sherd budget` for chains). The root chain is
# gated by the root file's row. A raise is its own commit with the
# measurement in `Why:`; the fix for an overage is to move rows down to
# the node that owns them, not to raise the number.
#
